# Ending — A Life in the Truth (BACKLOG § Endings, "the In-Fold Quiet Life").
# Modest, real, content within the frame. This ending must read as
# defensible: many real Witnesses live exactly this life and are not unhappy.
# TODO: authenticity check — ending draft.

Five years later.
You still sit in the same row, a little further back now that there are more of you. You met at an assembly. The wedding was at the Hall, and the reception ran late, and nobody minded.
{GameState.parent_word} watches the baby on meeting nights so the two of you can go together.
Some weeks are hard. Most weeks are just weeks.
if GameState.count("activity_visit_grandparent") > 0:
	{GameState.grandparent_word} lived to hold the baby. She hummed the song about the morning the whole afternoon, and fell asleep with her in her arms.
{GameState.sibling_name} is the fun uncle. He visits on weekday evenings, when there's no chance of a meeting, and nobody mentions that either.
On Saturdays you still go out. When a door opens, you smile first. You mean it.
